IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1984 (Western Australia) -- PART VII: STATUTORY POWERS AND DUTIES (ss 48 to 60).
-- Section 48A (judicial acts and service of process on any day) is in wa-interpretation-time.l4.
-- These sections say what a power, an office, a body or a delegation includes.  For the person the law is applied to
-- they decide: who may act against them (an acting officer, a delegate, a body without all its members), what the
-- authority may do (refuse a licence, impose conditions) and what is left to them (a right of appeal).

§ `Part VII -- Statutory powers and duties`

§§ `48. Time for exercise of power or performance of duty`

-- Section 48: where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be
-- performed from time to time as occasion requires.
-- src:557 | Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref s 48 (src:557)
GIVEN `a written law confers a power or imposes a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised and the duty performed from time to time as occasion requires` `a written law confers a power or imposes a duty` MEANS
    IF `a written law confers a power or imposes a duty` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `49. Public officer's powers and duties may be exercised by acting officer etc.`

DECLARE `Who is asked about under section 49` IS ONE OF
    `the person for the time being lawfully holding the office`
    `a person acting in the office`
    `a person performing the functions of the office`
    `a person who is none of these`

-- Section 49: where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of a public office as such, the power
-- may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the person for the time being lawfully holding, acting in, or
-- performing the functions of the office.  Another person is not dealt with (NOTHING).
-- src:565 | Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of a public office as such, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the person for the time being lawfully holding, acting in, or performing the functions of the office.
@ref s 49 (src:565)
GIVEN x IS A `Who is asked about under section 49`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person may exercise the power and must perform the duty of the public office` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `a person who is none of these` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `50. Statutory powers, construction of`

DECLARE `Power asked about under section 50(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a power to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate a matter`
    `a power to grant a licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption`
    `a power to approve a person, matter or thing`
    `a power to give directions`

DECLARE `Included power asked about under section 50(2)` IS ONE OF
    `to provide for the matter by licensing, registration or the granting of permits, and to prohibit acts whereby the prohibition, control or regulation might be evaded`
    `to impose reasonable conditions on the grant`
    `to withdraw the approval`
    `to express the directions in the form of prohibitions`

-- Section 50(1): where a written law confers on a person power to do or enforce the doing of any act or thing, all
-- such powers as are reasonably necessary to enable the person to do or enforce it are also deemed conferred.
-- Section 50(3): subject to s 3(3), the section applies to written laws passed or made after the commencement of this
-- Act; for any other law the section says nothing (NOTHING).  "Reasonably necessary" is a judgment: a plain input.
-- src:567 | (1) Where a written law confers upon a person power to do or enforce the doing of any act or thing, all such powers shall also be deemed to be conferred on the person as are reasonably necessary to enable him to do or to enforce the doing of the act or thing.
-- src:573 | (3) Subject to section 3(3), this section applies to written laws passed or made after the commencement of this Act.
@ref s 50(1) (src:567)
@ref s 50(3) (src:573)
GIVEN `the other power is reasonably necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the written law was passed or made` IS A DATE
      `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the other power is also deemed conferred` `the other power is reasonably necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the act or thing` `the day the written law was passed or made` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` MEANS
    IF `counts as passed or made after the commencement for ss 17, 25, 43(6), 50 and 64` `the day the written law was passed or made` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law`
    THEN JUST `the other power is reasonably necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the act or thing`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 50(2): without prejudice to (1), a power (a) to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate a matter includes
-- power to provide for it by licensing or registration or the granting of permits and to prohibit acts whereby the
-- prohibition, control or regulation might be evaded; (b) to grant a licence etc includes power to impose reasonable
-- conditions; (c) to approve a person, matter or thing includes power to withdraw approval; (d) to give directions
-- includes power to express them as prohibitions.  Each included power belongs with its own power; paired otherwise
-- the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:568 | (2) Without prejudice to the generality of subsection (1), where a written law confers power —
-- src:569 | (a) to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate any matter, such power includes power to provide for the same by the licensing or registration thereof or the granting of permits and power to prohibit acts whereby the prohibition, control, or regulation of such matter might be evaded;
-- src:570 | (b) to grant a licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval, or exemption, such power includes power to impose reasonable conditions subject to which such licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption may be granted;
-- src:571 | (c) to approve any person, matter, or thing, such power includes power to withdraw approval thereof;
-- src:572 | (d) to give directions, such power includes power to express the same in the form of prohibitions.
@ref s 50(2) (src:568-572)
GIVEN p IS A `Power asked about under section 50(2)`
      q IS A `Included power asked about under section 50(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power includes the other power` p q MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a power to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate a matter` THEN
        CONSIDER q
        WHEN `to provide for the matter by licensing, registration or the granting of permits, and to prohibit acts whereby the prohibition, control or regulation might be evaded` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `a power to grant a licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption` THEN
        CONSIDER q
        WHEN `to impose reasonable conditions on the grant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `a power to approve a person, matter or thing` THEN
        CONSIDER q
        WHEN `to withdraw the approval` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `a power to give directions` THEN
        CONSIDER q
        WHEN `to express the directions in the form of prohibitions` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `51. Power to issue licences and other authorisations is discretionary`

-- Section 51(1): where a written law confers power to issue, grant, give or renew a licence, registration, lease,
-- right, authority, approval, permit or exemption, the person empowered has a discretion either to issue, grant, give
-- or renew it or to refuse to.  So a person who applies is not entitled, by this section, to the grant.
-- src:575 | (1) Where a written law confers power upon a person to issue, grant, give or renew any licence, registration, lease, right, authority, approval, permit, or exemption, the person so empowered shall have a discretion either to issue, grant, give or renew or to refuse to issue, grant, give or renew such licence, registration, lease, right, authority, approval, permit, or exemption.
@ref s 51(1) (src:575)
GIVEN `a written law confers power to issue, grant, give or renew a licence or other authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person empowered has a discretion to grant or to refuse` `a written law confers power to issue, grant, give or renew a licence or other authorisation` MEANS
    IF `a written law confers power to issue, grant, give or renew a licence or other authorisation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 51(2): nothing in s 51 affects any right a written law confers to appeal against, apply for or seek a review
-- of a refusal.  The section creates no such right: it only leaves any that exists.
-- src:576 | (2) Nothing in this section shall affect any right which may be conferred by any written law upon a person to appeal against, or apply for or otherwise seek a review of, a refusal to issue, grant, give or renew any licence, registration, lease, right, authority, approval, permit, or exemption.
@ref s 51(2) (src:576)
GIVEN `a written law confers a right to appeal against, apply for or seek a review of a refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the right to appeal against or seek review of a refusal is left in place` `a written law confers a right to appeal against, apply for or seek a review of a refusal` MEANS
    IF `a written law confers a right to appeal against, apply for or seek a review of a refusal` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `52. Power to appoint includes power to remove, suspend, appoint acting officer etc.`

DECLARE `Power included in a power to appoint` IS ONE OF
    `to remove or suspend a person appointed`
    `to reappoint or reinstate a person appointed`
    `to appoint a person to act temporarily during a suspension or inability`
    `to specify the period for which a person appointed holds the appointment`
    `some other power`

DECLARE `Cause of inability asked about under section 52(2)` IS ONE OF
    `illness`
    `temporary absence from the State`
    `conflict of interest`
    `some other cause`

-- Section 52(1): where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty to make an appointment to an office or position,
-- including an acting appointment, the person having it also has the power (a) to remove or suspend, and to reappoint or
-- reinstate; (b) to appoint a person to act temporarily; (c) to specify the period of the appointment.  Another power is
-- not dealt with (NOTHING).
-- src:579 | (1) Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty upon a person to make an appointment to an office or position, including an acting appointment, the person having such power or duty shall also have the power —
-- src:580 | (a) to remove or suspend a person so appointed to an office or position, and to reappoint or reinstate, any person appointed in exercise of such power or duty; and
-- src:581 | (b) where a person so appointed to an office or position is suspended or unable, or expected to become unable, for any other cause to perform the functions of such office or position, to appoint a person to act temporarily in place of the person so appointed during the period of suspension or other inability but a person shall not be appointed to so act temporarily unless he is eligible and qualified to be appointed to the office or position; and
-- src:582 | (c) to specify the period for which any person appointed in exercise of such a power or duty shall hold his appointment.
@ref s 52(1) (src:579-582)
GIVEN x IS A `Power included in a power to appoint`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a power to appoint includes the power` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `some other power` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 52(1)(b): the temporary appointee must be eligible and qualified to be appointed to the office or position,
-- and the occasion is that the holder is suspended or unable, or expected to become unable, for any cause to perform the
-- functions.
@ref s 52(1)(b) (src:581)
GIVEN `the holder is suspended or unable, or expected to become unable, to perform the functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible and qualified to be appointed to the office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may be appointed to act temporarily` `the holder is suspended or unable, or expected to become unable, to perform the functions` `the person is eligible and qualified to be appointed to the office or position` MEANS
        `the holder is suspended or unable, or expected to become unable, to perform the functions`
    AND `the person is eligible and qualified to be appointed to the office or position`

-- Section 52(2): for s 52(1)(b), cause includes illness, temporary absence from the State, and conflict of interest.
-- src:583 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b), cause includes —
-- src:584 | (a) illness; and
-- src:585 | (b) temporary absence from the State; and
-- src:586 | (c) conflict of interest.
@ref s 52(2) (src:583-586)
GIVEN x IS A `Cause of inability asked about under section 52(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the cause is included in section 52(1)(b)` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `some other cause` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 52(3): the validity of anything done by a person purporting to act under such an acting appointment shall not
-- be called in question on the ground that the occasion for the appointment had not arisen or had ceased.  On any other
-- ground the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:587 | (3) The validity of anything done by a person purporting to act under an appointment made under subsection (1)(b) shall not be called in question on the ground that the occasion for his appointment had not arisen or had ceased.
@ref s 52(3) (src:587)
GIVEN `the ground is that the occasion for the appointment had not arisen or had ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the validity of the thing done can be called in question on that ground` `the ground is that the occasion for the appointment had not arisen or had ceased` MEANS
    IF `the ground is that the occasion for the appointment had not arisen or had ceased` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 52(4): where the power or duty to appoint is exercisable only on nomination or recommendation, or subject to
-- approval, concurrence or consent, the powers in (1)(a) to (c) are exercisable only on that nomination or
-- recommendation or subject to that approval, concurrence or consent.
-- src:588 | (4) Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty upon a person to make an appointment to an office or position and that power or duty is exercisable only upon the nomination or recommendation, or is subject to the approval, concurrence, or consent of some other person, then the powers conferred by subsection (1)(a) to (c) shall only be exercisable upon such nomination or recommendation or subject to such approval, concurrence, or consent.
@ref s 52(4) (src:588)
GIVEN `the power to appoint is exercisable only on nomination or recommendation, or subject to approval, concurrence or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nomination, recommendation, approval, concurrence or consent has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the powers in section 52(1)(a) to (c) are exercisable` `the power to appoint is exercisable only on nomination or recommendation, or subject to approval, concurrence or consent` `the nomination, recommendation, approval, concurrence or consent has been given` MEANS
        (NOT `the power to appoint is exercisable only on nomination or recommendation, or subject to approval, concurrence or consent`)
    OR  `the nomination, recommendation, approval, concurrence or consent has been given`

-- Section 52(5): nothing in s 52 affects the tenure of office or position of any person under the express provisions of
-- any written law.
-- src:589 | (5) Nothing in this section affects the tenure of office or position of any person under the express provisions of any written law.
@ref s 52(5) (src:589)
GIVEN `a written law expressly provides for the tenure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 52 affects the tenure` `a written law expressly provides for the tenure` MEANS FALSE

§§ `53. Appointments may be by name or office`

-- Section 53: a power or duty to appoint or designate a person to perform a function, be a member of a board or similar
-- body, or be or do any other thing may be exercised by naming the person or by appointing or designating the holder of
-- an office; the latter is construed as the appointment of the person from time to time holding, acting in, or lawfully
-- performing the functions of the office.
-- src:592 | Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty upon a person to appoint or designate a person to —
-- src:593 | (a) perform any function; or
-- src:594 | (b) be a member of any board, tribunal, commission, committee, council, or other similar body, whether corporate or unincorporate; or
-- src:595 | (c) be or do any other thing,
-- src:596 | that person may make the appointment or designation either by appointing or designating a person by name or by appointing or designating the holder of an office by the term designating his office; and any such appointment or designation of the holder of an office shall be construed as the appointment or designation of the person from time to time holding, acting in, or lawfully performing the functions of the office.
@ref s 53 (src:592-596)
GIVEN `the appointment is of the holder of an office by the term designating the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointment is of the person from time to time holding, acting in, or performing the functions of the office` `the appointment is of the holder of an office by the term designating the office` MEANS
    `the appointment is of the holder of an office by the term designating the office`

§§ `54. Statutory bodies, majority and quorum provisions`

-- Section 54(1): where a written law confers or imposes a function on a body or number of persons consisting of not
-- fewer than 3 persons, the function may be performed by a majority of those persons.  For fewer than 3 the section
-- says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:598 | (1) Where a written law confers or imposes a function upon a body or number of persons consisting of not fewer than 3 persons, the function may be performed by a majority of those persons.
@ref s 54(1) (src:598)
GIVEN `the number of persons` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them who agree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the function may be performed by those who agree` `the number of persons` `the number of them who agree` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons` AT LEAST 3
    THEN JUST (`the number of them who agree` GREATER THAN `the number of persons` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 54(2)(a)(i): for a board, commission, committee, council or similar body of 3 or more members (an
-- "association") with a fixed number of members, a quorum is a number of members equal to at least one half of the
-- number provided for by the written law.  At least half of 5 is 2.5, so 3 members (fork F9 in NOTES.md).
-- src:599 | (2) Where a written law establishes a board, commission, committee, council or other similar body consisting of 3 or more members (in this section called an association) —
-- src:600 | (a) at a meeting of the association, a number of members of the association equal to —
-- src:601 | (i) at least one half of the number of members provided for by the written law, if that number is a fixed number; and
-- src:602 | (ii) if the number of members provided for by the written law is not a fixed number but is within a range having a maximum or minimum, at least one half of the number of members in office if that number is within the range,
-- src:603 | constitutes a quorum; and
@ref s 54(2) (src:599)
@ref s 54(2)(a)(i) (src:601)
@ref s 54(2)(a) (src:603)
GIVEN `the number of members the written law provides for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the least number of members that make a quorum, with a fixed number of members` `the number of members the written law provides for` MEANS
    IF `the number of members the written law provides for` AT LEAST 3
    THEN JUST (CEILING (`the number of members the written law provides for` DIVIDED BY 2))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 54(2)(a)(ii): where the number provided for is not fixed but is within a range having a maximum or minimum, a
-- quorum is at least one half of the number of members in office, if that number is within the range.
@ref s 54(2)(a)(ii) (src:602)
GIVEN `the number of members in office` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members in office is within the range` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the least number of members that make a quorum, with a range of members` `the number of members in office` `the number of members in office is within the range` MEANS
    IF `the number of members in office is within the range`
    THEN JUST (CEILING (`the number of members in office` DIVIDED BY 2))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 54(2)(b): an act or thing done by a majority of the members present at a meeting, if the members present
-- constitute a quorum, is deemed to have been done by the association.
-- src:604 | (b) an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the association present at a meeting, if the members present constitute a quorum, shall be deemed to have been done by the association.
@ref s 54(2)(b) (src:604)
GIVEN `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members present who agree` IS A NUMBER
      `the least number of members that make a quorum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the act is deemed done by the association` `the number of members present` `the number of members present who agree` `the least number of members that make a quorum` MEANS
        `the number of members present` AT LEAST `the least number of members that make a quorum`
    AND `the number of members present who agree` GREATER THAN `the number of members present` DIVIDED BY 2

§§ `55. Errors when exercising certain powers or duties may be corrected`

-- Section 55: where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty to do an act or thing of an administrative or
-- executive character or to make an appointment, the power or duty may be exercised or performed as often as is
-- necessary to correct any error or omission in a previous purported exercise or performance, even though it is not in
-- general capable of being exercised or performed from time to time.
-- src:606 | Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty upon a person to do any act or thing of an administrative or executive character or to make any appointment, the power or duty may be exercised or performed as often as is necessary to correct any error or omission in any previous purported exercise or performance of the power or duty, notwithstanding that the power or duty is not in general capable of being exercised or performed from time to time.
@ref s 55 (src:606)
GIVEN `the act is of an administrative or executive character, or is the making of an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power or duty may be exercised again as often as is necessary to correct an error or omission` `the act is of an administrative or executive character, or is the making of an appointment` MEANS
    IF `the act is of an administrative or executive character, or is the making of an appointment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `56. "May" imports a discretion, "shall" is imperative`

DECLARE `Word used in conferring a power or function` IS ONE OF
    `the word may, in conferring a power`
    `the word shall, in conferring a function`

DECLARE `What the word means` IS ONE OF
    `the power may be exercised or not, at discretion`
    `the function must be performed`

-- Section 56(1) and (2): the word may used in conferring a power implies the power may be exercised or not, at
-- discretion; the word shall used in conferring a function means the function must be performed.
-- src:608 | (1) Where in a written law the word may is used in conferring a power, such word shall be interpreted to imply that the power so conferred may be exercised or not, at discretion.
-- src:609 | (2) Where in a written law the word shall is used in conferring a function, such word shall be interpreted to mean that the function so conferred must be performed.
@ref s 56(1) (src:608)
@ref s 56(2) (src:609)
GIVEN w IS A `Word used in conferring a power or function`
GIVETH A `What the word means`
`what the word means` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `the word may, in conferring a power` THEN `the power may be exercised or not, at discretion`
    WHEN `the word shall, in conferring a function` THEN `the function must be performed`

§§ `57. Statutory bodies, powers of not affected by vacancies etc.`

DECLARE `Defect in a statutory body` IS ONE OF
    `a vacancy in the membership of the body`
    `a defect afterwards discovered in the appointment or qualification of a person purporting to be a member, deputy or alternate`
    `a minor irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting`
    `the presence or participation at a meeting of a person not entitled to be present or participate`
    `a major irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting`

-- Section 57: the powers of a board, tribunal, commission, committee, council or similar body established under a written
-- law are not affected by (a) a vacancy; (b) a defect afterwards discovered in a member's appointment or qualification;
-- (c) a minor irregularity in convening or conducting a meeting; (d) the presence or participation of a person not
-- entitled.  A major irregularity is not dealt with (NOTHING).
-- src:611 | Where a board, tribunal, commission, committee, council or other similar body, whether corporate or unincorporate, is established under a written law, the powers of such a body shall not be affected by —
-- src:612 | (a) any vacancy in the membership of the body; or
-- src:613 | (b) any defect afterwards discovered in the appointment or qualification of a person purporting to be a member of the body or the deputy or alternate of a member; or
-- src:614 | (c) a minor irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting of the body; or
-- src:615 | (d) the presence or participation at a meeting of a person not entitled to be present or participate.
@ref s 57 (src:611-615)
GIVEN x IS A `Defect in a statutory body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the powers of the body are affected by` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `a major irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `58. Delegates, performance of functions by`

DECLARE `Whose state of mind counts` IS ONE OF
    `the delegate's`
    `the person's who delegated`

-- Section 58: where performance of a function depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of a person and the
-- function has been delegated under a written law, the function may be performed by the delegate upon the opinion,
-- belief or state of mind of the delegate.
-- src:617 | Where under a written law the performance of a function by a person is dependent upon the opinion, belief, or state of mind of that person in relation to a matter and that function has been delegated under a written law, the function may be performed by the delegate upon the opinion, belief, or state of mind of the delegate in relation to that matter.
@ref s 58 (src:617)
GIVEN `the function has been delegated under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whose state of mind counts`
`whose opinion, belief or state of mind counts` `the function has been delegated under a written law` MEANS
    IF `the function has been delegated under a written law` THEN `the delegate's` ELSE `the person's who delegated`

§§ `59. Power to delegate, effect of`

DECLARE `Feature of a delegation` IS ONE OF
    `the delegator may still exercise or perform the power or duty delegated, at any time`
    `it may be made subject to conditions, qualifications, limitations or exceptions the delegator specifies`
    `where it needs another person's approval, it and any amendment of it may be made subject to the conditions that person specifies`
    `it may be made to a specified person, to persons of a specified class, or to the holder or holders for the time being of a specified office or class of office`
    `it may be amended or revoked by instrument in writing signed by the delegator`
    `where the power is conferred by reference to an office, it does not cease to have effect only because the person acting in the office changes`
    `some other feature`

-- Section 59(1): where a written law confers power to delegate, (a) to (f).  A feature not listed is not dealt with
-- (NOTHING).
-- src:619 | (1) Where a written law confers power upon a person to delegate the exercise of any power or the performance of any duty conferred or imposed upon him under a written law —
-- src:620 | (a) such a delegation shall not preclude a person so delegating from exercising or performing at any time a power or duty so delegated;
-- src:621 | (b) such a delegation may be made subject to such conditions, qualifications, limitations or exceptions as the person so delegating may specify;
-- src:622 | (c) if the delegation may be made only with the approval of some person, such delegation, and any amendment of the delegation, may be made subject to such conditions, qualifications, limitations or exceptions as the person whose approval is required may specify;
-- src:623 | (d) such a delegation may be made to a specified person or to persons of a specified class, or may be made to the holder or holders for the time being of a specified office or class of office;
-- src:624 | (e) such a delegation may be amended or revoked by instrument in writing signed by the person so delegating;
-- src:625 | (f) in the case of a power conferred upon a person by reference to the term designating an office, such a delegation shall not cease to have effect by reason only of a change in the person lawfully acting in or performing the functions of that office.
@ref s 59(1) (src:619-625)
GIVEN x IS A `Feature of a delegation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a delegation has the feature` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `some other feature` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 59(2): the delegation of a power is deemed to include the delegation of any duty incidental or connected with
-- it, and the delegation of a duty is deemed to include the delegation of any power incidental or connected with it.
-- src:626 | (2) The delegation of a power shall be deemed to include the delegation of any duty incidental thereto or connected therewith and the delegation of a duty shall be deemed to include the delegation of any power incidental thereto or connected therewith.
@ref s 59(2) (src:626)
GIVEN `the other function is incidental to, or connected with, the one delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the other function is deemed delegated too` `the other function is incidental to, or connected with, the one delegated` MEANS
    `the other function is incidental to, or connected with, the one delegated`

-- Section 59(3): where an act or thing may or must be done to, by reference to, or in relation to a person, and that
-- person has delegated a relevant function, the act is regarded as effectually done if done to, by reference to, or in
-- relation to the delegate.
-- src:627 | (3) Where under a written law an act or thing may or is required to be done to, by reference to or in relation to, a person and that person has under a written law delegated a relevant function conferred or imposed on him with respect to or in consequence of the doing of that act or thing, the act or thing shall be regarded as effectually done if done to, by reference to or in relation to the person to whom the function has been delegated.
@ref s 59(3) (src:627)
GIVEN `the person has delegated a relevant function under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is done to, by reference to, or in relation to the delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the act is regarded as effectually done` `the person has delegated a relevant function under a written law` `the act is done to, by reference to, or in relation to the delegate` MEANS
    IF `the person has delegated a relevant function under a written law` AND `the act is done to, by reference to, or in relation to the delegate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `60. Governor to act with advice of Executive Council`

-- Section 60: where in a written law the Governor is authorised or required to do any act, matter or thing, it is taken
-- to mean that it may or shall be done by the Governor with the advice and consent of the Executive Council.
-- src:629 | Where in a written law the Governor is authorised or required to do any act, matter, or thing, it shall be taken to mean that such act, matter, or thing may or shall be done by the Governor with the advice and consent of the Executive Council.
@ref s 60 (src:629)
GIVEN `the Governor is authorised or required to do the act, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is done by the Governor with the advice and consent of the Executive Council` `the Governor is authorised or required to do the act, matter or thing` MEANS
    IF `the Governor is authorised or required to do the act, matter or thing` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
